    "notes": [
      "deck_empty keeps the door's frame and smoke baked in, as the photo saw it.",
      "door_frame / door_glass redraw the door over a tape; over the empty well the glass would tint twice, so draw them only when a tape is shown or the door moves.",
      "VU pivots are the scale-arc centres, below the faces (hidden by the hub dome); draw the needle from the pivot and clip it to the face.",
      "glows: glow_play.png / glow_pause.png are the lit key rows (lamp strip, the glow in the gap above it, the warm faceplate edge) drawn NORMAL (source-over) at the rect over deck_empty_v2, whose PLAY is unlit. Opacity 1 = the photo lit key; animate opacity to fade the lamp. Not additive: see scripts/mixtape/edit_deck_plate.py.",
      "knob: knob.png is the face only (radius and spriteSize are fractions of the plate HEIGHT; the sprite is centred on center). Rotate it clockwise by (target - dotAngleDeg), where target = minAngleDeg + volume * (maxAngleDeg - minAngleDeg). The plate under it is the same face without the dot. Alternative: leave the face static and rotate knob_dot.png (same canvas) instead, which keeps the cone-brushed highlights fixed as on a real knob."
